course: dictionary
lesson: 11485
title: Afflicted: suffering from trouble
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Afflicted» means suffering from an illness, pain or trouble. «The old man was afflicted with a bad cough all winter.» The words «with a bad cough» tell you what he was suffering from, so afflicted means he was ill and it hurt him.
explain: Afflicted is also the past form of the verb «afflict», which means to cause someone pain or trouble. «The village was afflicted by floods last spring.» The floods caused the trouble, and the village was the place that suffered it.
explain: You may also see «the afflicted» in a text. This means people who suffer, as in «We must help the afflicted.» Look at the words around it to find out who is suffering and why.
fact: Afflicted means suffering from an illness, pain or trouble.
fact: «Afflict» means to cause someone pain or trouble, and afflicted is its past form.
fact: Common phrases are «afflicted with», as in an illness, and «afflicted by», as in a disaster such as floods or drought.
fact: «The afflicted» is a formal way to say people who suffer.
fact: The Bible speaks of comforting the afflicted, which means helping people who are suffering.
exercise: «The little girl was afflicted with a fever and stayed in bed.» What does afflicted mean here? | Lost in a big city | *Suffering from an illness | Running fast in the park | Very happy and full of energy
exercise: «The afflicted families waited for help after the storm.» Find and copy one word that shows people were suffering. | storm | *afflicted | families | waited
exercise: Ben says afflicted is a fancy word for happy. Is he right? | *No, it means suffering from trouble or illness | Yes, it means happy and joyful | Yes, it means lucky | No, it means very quiet
test: «The farmers were afflicted by drought all summer.» Who had the trouble? | The bread | The summer | *The farmers | The rain
test: What does «comfort the afflicted» mean? | Make people laugh loudly | Tell people a secret | *Help people who are suffering | Give people new shoes
exam: Which sentence uses afflicted to mean suffering from an illness? | «The sun was afflicted with a smile.» | «He afflicted his bike with a new bell.» | «The bus was afflicted by a bright red colour.» | *«She was afflicted with a sore throat.»
